    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1379">

                <pb facs="0918" n="802" xml:id="pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/222.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Carothers to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Carranza undoubtedly gave statement to press to effect that property of Spaniards
                    will not be confiscated. I fear he will take no action with Villa considering
                    his former statement to me that he would not interfere with the orders given by
                    Villa. Cotton belonging to Spaniards and others, among it six cars belonging to
                    Purcell and Co., is beginning to arrive in Juarez. I believe Carranza will go to
                    Chihuahua to meet Villa who will go there from Torreon about Sunday, the 12th. I
                    believe he will take no action whatever until after the meeting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G C. Carothers</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
